<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: National Irish Bank raises mortgage rates 0.4 pct.</title>
<headline>National Irish Bank raises mortgage rates 0.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Irish Bank said on Friday that it was raising its variable mortgage rate by 0.4 percent with effect from the close of business on Monday September 9.</p>
<p>Variable rate mortgages will increase to 7.10 percent from 6.7 percent, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>NIB said it was also increasing its AA term loan and overdraft rates by a similar amount.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9775</p>
